---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import execution from './execution.json';
import './recovery.css';
const disconnect=execution.client_events.find(e=>e.action==='disconnect')!.seconds;
const stored=execution.engine_events.find(e=>e.kind==='engine_log'&&e.message?.includes('stored in Redis'))!.seconds;
const recovered=execution.client_events.find(e=>e.action==='retrieve_response')!.seconds;
const checkpoints=[{name:'Connected',time:0},{name:'Disconnected',time:disconnect},{name:'Stored',time:stored},{name:'Recovered',time:recovered}];
---
<section class="rl" data-recovery-lab data-phase="ready" aria-labelledby="rl-title">
  <script id="rl-data" type="application/json" set:html={JSON.stringify(execution).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')} />
  <div class="rl-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Recorded execution / interactive replay</p><h2 id="rl-title">One turn. <em>Two views.</em></h2></div><p>Replay the actual 14 October run. Controls move the recording; they make no live request.</p></div>
  <div class="rl-task"><span class="rl-task-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="asterisk" /></span><div><span class="eyebrow">The fictional task</span><p>Prepare the opening checklist for the Lantern Makers Club.</p></div><span class="rl-task-scope">No tools · No private data</span></div>
  <div class="rl-command"><button class="rl-primary" data-action="play">Play the recorded task <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></button><button data-action="disconnect">Jump to disconnect</button><button data-action="recover" disabled>Replay answer retrieval</button><button class="rl-reset" data-action="reset" aria-label="Reset replay"><Icon name="rotate" /></button></div>
  <div class="rl-outcome" aria-live="polite" data-status>Start the replay, or jump to the moment the connection closed.</div>
  <div class="rl-mobile-comparison" aria-label="Recorded client and engine comparison"><p><span>Browser client</span><strong data-mobile-client>0 characters</strong><small data-mobile-client-state>Ready</small></p><p><span>Engine & storage</span><strong data-mobile-engine>0 characters</strong><small data-mobile-engine-state>Ready</small></p></div>
  <div class="rl-stage">
    <article class="rl-client"><header><span class="rl-lane-label">01 / Browser client</span><span class="rl-state" data-client-state>Ready</span></header><div class="rl-browser-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>fictional workshop task</span></div><div class="rl-client-body"><p class="rl-placeholder" data-placeholder>The answer will begin here.</p><div class="rl-answer" data-answer tabindex="0" aria-label="Recorded browser answer"></div><div class="rl-freeze-note" data-freeze-note hidden><span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="pause" /></span><p>The client has stopped receiving.<br />The engine hasn’t stopped working.</p></div></div><footer><span data-client-count>0 characters received</span><span data-client-route>POST /stream</span></footer></article>
    <div class="rl-link" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 70 360"><path class="rl-cable" d="M0 120 C35 120 35 120 70 120"/><circle class="rl-packet" cx="35" cy="120" r="5"/><path class="rl-cut" d="m28 112 14 16m-14 0 14-16"/><path class="rl-return" d="M70 260 C35 260 35 260 0 260"/><path class="rl-arrow" d="m12 253-10 7 10 7"/></svg><span data-link-label>SSE</span></div>
    <article class="rl-engine"><header><span class="rl-lane-label">02 / Engine & Redis</span><span class="rl-state" data-engine-state>Ready</span></header><div class="rl-machine"><div class="rl-rotor" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Same engine process</span><p data-machine-state>Waiting for the task</p><strong data-engine-count>0</strong><span class="rl-unit"> answer characters</span></div></div><div class="rl-storage"><span class="rl-storage-light" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><span class="eyebrow">Stored result</span><p data-storage-state>Awaiting completion</p></div><span data-storage-code>—</span></div><ol class="rl-log" data-events aria-label="Observed engine events"><li>Actual Claude subscription inference</li><li>Original route & result storage code</li><li>Isolated local Redis · delivery worker off</li></ol><footer><span>Disconnect policy: <strong>hold</strong></span><span>0 tool calls</span></footer></article>
  </div>
  <div class="rl-timeline"><div class="rl-time-head"><label for="rl-playhead">Recorded time</label><output data-clock for="rl-playhead">0.00s</output><span>{recovered.toFixed(2)}s to retrieval</span></div><input id="rl-playhead" data-playhead type="range" min="0" max={recovered} step="0.001" value="0" aria-label="Scrub the recorded execution" /><div class="rl-checkpoints">{checkpoints.map(point=><button data-seek={point.time}><span>{point.name}</span><small>{point.time.toFixed(2)}s</small></button>)}</div></div>
  <div class="rl-proof-strip"><p><strong>{execution.checks.partial_characters}</strong><span>characters before disconnect</span></p><span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-right" /></span><p><strong>{execution.checks.recovered_characters.toLocaleString('en')}</strong><span>characters recovered</span></p><p><strong>202 <Icon name="arrow-right" /> 200</strong><span>running, then completed</span></p><p><strong>Same answer</strong><span>two successful reads</span></p></div>
  <details class="rl-receipt"><summary>Inspect the execution receipt <span>Source, timestamps & boundaries <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></summary><div class="rl-receipt-grid"><div><h3>What ran</h3><p>Claude Engine’s actual HTTP routes, invocation, client pool and bundled SDK CLI, with real Redis. The browser aborted its fetch stream. The engine detected the failed write and stored the final answer after the same turn completed.</p><dl><dt>Source revision</dt><dd><code>{execution.source_revision}</code></dd><dt>Captured</dt><dd>14 October 2026 · 21:29 UTC</dd><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>Sonnet 5.5 · SDK 0.2.164 · Redis 7.0.15</dd><dt>Final answer SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{execution.result_sha256}</code></dd></dl><a class="text-link" href="/media/recovery/execution-receipt.json" download>Download the redacted receipt <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-down" /></span></a></div><div><h3>What the harness changed</h3><p>Service setup was restricted to the local experiment. MCP connections, workflow shipping, background restore and notification delivery were disabled. The original outbox enqueue wrote its receipt locally, with no delivery worker.</p><p>A temporary configuration directory contained only subscription auth and this fictional session. The engine’s session index was redirected into it. The owned auth copy was removed after capture. Paid API keys were excluded from the environment.</p><h3 class="rl-boundary-title">The tested boundary</h3><p><strong>A client connection closed while the engine kept running.</strong> This run did not test a process restart, conversation migration, tool approvals or production client reconciliation. The exhibit replays recorded evidence; it does not make a live model request.</p></div></div></details>
</section>
<script>import './controller';</script>
